WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.001 --> 00:00:05.666
Alice and the Gryphon rushed into the courtroom.

2
00:00:05.667 --> 00:00:11.897
A large crowd had gathered—birds, animals, and the whole pack of cards.

3
00:00:11.898 --> 00:00:15.864
The King and Queen of Hearts were seated on their thrones.

4
00:00:15.865 --> 00:00:20.015
The Knave of Hearts stood in front of his parents.

5
00:00:20.016 --> 00:00:24.208
He was in chains with two soldiers guarding him.

6
00:00:24.209 --> 00:00:29.204
"It must be the Knave's trial," Alice said to the Gryphon as they sat down.

7
00:00:29.205 --> 00:00:32.409
"Oh, look! There's the White Rabbit."

8
00:00:32.410 --> 00:00:36.034
The White Rabbit seemed to be a court official.

9
00:00:36.035 --> 00:00:42.441
Holding a trumpet in one hand, he clutched a scroll of paper in the other.

10
00:00:42.442 --> 00:00:47.283
Alice noticed a dish of tarts on a table.

11
00:00:47.284 --> 00:00:51.549
"Those tarts are making me hungry," she said to the Gryphon.

12
00:00:51.550 --> 00:00:54.827
"I wish this trial was over, so we could eat them."

13
00:00:54.828 --> 00:00:59.004
"That won't happen for quite a while," the Gryphon replied.

14
00:00:59.005 --> 00:01:02.657
Alice looked around the room.

15
00:01:02.658 --> 00:01:07.963
Although she'd never been in a courtroom before, she'd read about trials.

16
00:01:07.964 --> 00:01:13.694
"The King is wearing a long wig, so he's the judge," she said to herself.

17
00:01:13.695 --> 00:01:18.568
"And over there is the jury box, and those 12 creatures are the jurors."

18
00:01:18.569 --> 00:01:22.169
The jurors were busy writing on slates.

19
00:01:22.170 --> 00:01:25.545
"What are they doing?" Alice whispered to the Gryphon.

20
00:01:25.546 --> 00:01:30.472
"The trial hasn't started, so there's nothing for them to write down."

21
00:01:30.473 --> 00:01:32.829
"They're writing their names.

22
00:01:32.830 --> 00:01:37.006
They don't want to forget their names before the end of the trial."

23
00:01:37.007 --> 00:01:42.357
"What?" Alice said in a loud voice. "Stupid creatures!"

24
00:01:42.358 --> 00:01:49.460
She stopped talking because the White Rabbit cried, "Silence in the court!"

25
00:01:49.461 --> 00:01:54.925
The King put on his glasses and looked around to see who was still talking.

26
00:01:54.926 --> 00:01:57.343
Alice stayed quiet.

27
00:01:57.344 --> 00:02:06.353
From her seat, she could see the jurors writing, "Stupid creatures!"

28
00:02:06.354 --> 00:02:11.553
"Their slates will be full before the trial starts," Alice thought.

29
00:02:11.554 --> 00:02:19.502
"White Rabbit, tell us what the prisoner is accused of," the King said.

30
00:02:19.503 --> 00:02:23.703
The White Rabbit blew three blasts on his trumpet.

31
00:02:23.704 --> 00:02:27.928
Then he unrolled his scroll and began to read:

32
00:02:27.929 --> 00:02:31.507
The Queen of Hearts, she made some tarts,

33
00:02:31.508 --> 00:02:34.371
All on a summer day.

34
00:02:34.372 --> 00:02:38.332
The Knave of Hearts, he stole those tarts,

35
00:02:38.333 --> 00:02:43.397
And took them quite away!

36
00:02:43.398 --> 00:02:48.027
"What is your verdict?" the King asked the jury.

37
00:02:48.028 --> 00:02:51.203
"Not yet!" the White Rabbit said.

38
00:02:51.204 --> 00:02:55.411
"We need to hear from the witnesses."

39
00:02:55.412 --> 00:02:59.846
"Call the first witness," the King said.

40
00:02:59.847 --> 00:03:06.996
The White Rabbit blew three more blasts on his trumpet. "First witness!" he called.

41
00:03:06.997 --> 00:03:10.048
The first witness was the Hatter.

42
00:03:10.049 --> 00:03:13.237
He arrived with a teacup in one hand.

43
00:03:13.238 --> 00:03:16.103
He held bread and butter in the other.

44
00:03:16.104 --> 00:03:21.272
"I beg your pardon for bringing these, Your Majesty," he said.

45
00:03:21.273 --> 00:03:25.878
"But I hadn't quite finished my tea when I was sent for."

46
00:03:25.879 --> 00:03:30.758
"You should have finished your tea," the King said.

47
00:03:30.759 --> 00:03:34.750
"When did you begin drinking it?"

48
00:03:34.751 --> 00:03:40.857
The Hatter looked at the March Hare and the Dormouse, who had followed him in.

49
00:03:40.858 --> 00:03:46.394
"I think it was March 14th," the Hatter said.

50
00:03:46.395 --> 00:03:50.712
"Fifteenth," the March Hare corrected him.

51
00:03:50.713 --> 00:03:54.891
"Sixteenth," the Dormouse said.

52
00:03:54.892 --> 00:04:00.054
"Write that down," the King said to the jury.

53
00:04:00.055 --> 00:04:05.462
The creatures in the jury box eagerly wrote down all three dates.

54
00:04:05.463 --> 00:04:11.669
Then they added them together and divided by five.

55
00:04:11.670 --> 00:04:14.858
Meanwhile the Queen put on her glasses.

56
00:04:14.859 --> 00:04:19.971
She stared at the Hatter, who turned pale.

57
00:04:19.972 --> 00:04:27.051
"Tell your story, and don't be nervous," the King said to the Hatter.

58
00:04:27.052 --> 00:04:32.101
"Or I'll have your head cut off."

59
00:04:32.102 --> 00:04:34.385
This didn't help the Hatter.

60
00:04:34.386 --> 00:04:39.400
He nervously took a bite from his teacup instead of his bread.

61
00:04:39.401 --> 00:04:44.118
Just then Alice felt a strange sensation.

62
00:04:44.119 --> 00:04:47.035
"What's going on?" she thought.

63
00:04:47.036 --> 00:04:50.074
But then she realized what was happening.

64
00:04:50.075 --> 00:04:58.004
"I'm growing again, and I haven't even eaten a bite of those tarts!"

